#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354261 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179677 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2e71ba74-f952-56ef-885c-a32c4a4aec20" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Logistic Growth Initial Value Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a7d2a3a-2e9b-513d-aefc-deb7330c3256" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{8\\,000}{1+4{e}^{-0.1t}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351658} {:answer/id #uuid "2bd4e14d-f873-5392-91f7-897cf31de18f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{8\\,000}{1+4{e}^{-2t}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351965} {:answer/id #uuid "c73b56a5-cac1-5b5a-8072-9761fae2a107" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{8\\,000}{1+5{e}^{-0.5t}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353293} {:answer/id #uuid "da7e22be-49d9-5065-8d9b-091acb94dba2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{8\\,000}{1+7{e}^{-0.5t}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353464} {:answer/id #uuid "e700e7cb-c861-580f-9a2b-f525130e76a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{8\\,000}{1+5{e}^{-0.2t}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353579}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da7e22be-49d9-5065-8d9b-091acb94dba2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{8\\,000}{1+7{e}^{-0.5t}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353464} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ce8c811-8797-5860-954a-946f44e6804b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353981}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2c1c2a21-498a-5ae4-81c4-0f8dccba7406" :question/math-academy-id "q-83875" :question/problem "The growth rate of the mouse population $P(t)$ in a certain field is jointly proportional to the mouse population at time $t,$ measured in years, and the difference between the field's carrying capacity and the mouse population. If the constant of proportionality is $0.000\\,062\\,5$ and the carrying capacity is $8\\,000,$ then find an expression for the mouse population after $t$ years, given that there were $1\\,000$ mice in the field initially." :question/worked-solution "Since the mouse population's growth rate is *jointly* proportional to the mouse population at time $t$ and the difference between the carrying capacity and the mouse population, the mouse population follows a logistic growth model.\n\nA logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nThe general solution to the logistic growth equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{a}{1+C{e}^{-akt}}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the constant of proportionality is $k=0.000\\,062\\,5,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=8\\,000.$ Therefore, the mouse population growth is given by the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.000\\,062\\,5P(8\\,000-P).\n$$\n\nThe general solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{8\\,000}{1+C{e}^{-(8\\,000\\cdot 0.000\\,062\\,5)t}}=\\frac{8\\,000}{1+C{e}^{-0.5t}}.\n$$\n\nWe now substitute the initial condition $P(0)=1\\,000$ and solve for $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8\\,000}{1+C{e}^{-0.5\\cdot 0}} & =1\\,000 \\\\ 1+C & =\\frac{8\\,000}{1\\,000} \\\\ C & =8-1 \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(t)=\\frac{8\\,000}{1+7{e}^{-0.5t}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
